    {
      "id": "claim_5aaad6b2d2e041b085523b0cb6fac658",
      "statement": "distinctive_tokens() picks non-generic tokens in order, deduplicated and capped at TAG_LIMIT=3, for tag-based API queries; unlike signal_tokens it tokenizes the raw query (query.lower()) rather than canon(query), so it sees literal words not aliased forms; it returns the words that narrow the search and empty means the caller should ask without a tag.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L170-L183",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:416ef07d315ea431c11c2312c090960173aa1489a8671d5cac2605f182c99e4a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_67a5ddeba80547c8b2a098e089e01adb",
      "statement": "title_hit uses regex r'\\b{token}(?:js|s|\\d+)?\\b' matching whole words with optional plural/version/js suffix; there is no <4 char special case. Suffixes are allowed (python3, reactjs, agents) but prefixes are not (rust does not match anti-trust, java does not match javascript).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L192-L200",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9be826f93953bd3893d7519b825061d4d7e8dbb27510cafdb059e53168bc7fd1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_24f697c1fa184b7f8f238b9ee14891cd",
      "statement": "score_job is frequency-weighted: title_hits*TITLE_WEIGHT plus a description contribution of min(desc_hits + gen_hits + freq/8, 9), where gen_hits counts GENERIC words in the title (0 when the whole query is generic) and freq/8 is a frequency bonus; the description is canon-normalized before desc_words/desc_hits/freq are computed. The description contribution is capped at 9, below TITLE_WEIGHT=10, so it can only reorder admitted results, never admit a job the title did not match.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L203-L222",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:03c56a9b89df58e70e4b7e78c5a2f3a66d58fabdacc5b7d180d17948ffb8c0cb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cea7bf93376b4f4ca4b6ddf6cf0dd397",
      "statement": "collect_results deduplicates by a company+title hash (re.sub removing non-alphanumeric) rather than apply_url, keeps only jobs passing location_ok(job, country) and job_is_recent(job) (MAX_AGE_DAYS=120), keeps score >= TITLE_WEIGHT, applies a wants_engineer special case (when title_hit('engineer', canon(query)) the job title must also contain 'engineer'), sorts by score descending, and caps at MAX_RESULTS=12; after capping it strip_html-cleans and truncates each description to 2000 characters.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L577-L610",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1f1374fee1cd2b78caa0f10766671c10bffca979adc7b467278191d28385c068:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_370c8c720e44439ca5b8c377533dc377",
      "statement": "fetch_wjobs (Workable) is a two-round crawl: workable_urls fetches search pages and extracts links from schema.org ItemList LD+JSON using path-form URLs (/search/<country>/remote-<token>-jobs) because robots.txt disallows the query-string form; the country segment is mandatory ('worldwide' slug) and an unknown country returns 200 with an empty list, retried worldwide. workable_job then fetches each surviving posting's JobPosting LD+JSON block, capped at WORKABLE_DETAILS=6 per-posting fetches.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L411-L509",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e1e29581984f404f8bec9478b9dbc564009edbea83e06d30c18386d56da1f79:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7ddc1b6138b14078bb2c33a07b3e5f2e",
      "statement": "fetch_jobs (RemoteOK) uses distinctive_tokens (not just the first keyword), tries tags in order until a page returns >= ENOUGH (50) results, deduplicates by URL/id across tag attempts, and re-checks every listing against its own title via title_hit because RemoteOK tags are SEO filler.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L280-L308",
